# Nothing regenerable is tracked. `make all` rebuilds this project end to end
# from the R scripts alone (~6 s, ~10 MB downloaded) — see R/00_prepare_data.R.

# Raw Météo-France source data — downloaded on demand by stage 00 from the
# mirror in R/config.R (MF_BASE_URL). Public, Licence Ouverte, no credentials.
# NOTE: the upstream filenames encode years and rotate each January; bump
#       MF_ERAS in R/config.R when the cycle turns.
data/raw/

# Cached station extract + intermediates — regenerable via `make prepare`
data/processed/

# Generated analysis outputs — rebuilt by `make all`.
# The report is the shareable artifact: copy it out, do not commit it (a 2 MB
# base64 HTML re-inflates the history on every refresh).
# EXCEPTION: the three PNG figures ARE tracked. README.md renders the report
# inline (see R/03_readme.R) and GitHub can only show the figures if they live
# in the repository. Keep the figure commit as an amend of the existing history
# entry rather than a new commit, so refreshes don't stack up PNG blobs.
outputs/*
!outputs/figures/
outputs/figures/*
!outputs/figures/*.png

# R session cruft
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# macOS
.DS_Store

# AI assistant & editor helper artifacts — never commit (local configs / home setup)
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
